The first thing '''Ivo Ren''' changed was a bell.

In Leth, everyone remembered hearing it during the river evacuation. The streets had emptied; a child had been carried out of a flooded room. Yet the municipal log had no order to ring it, no person who had pulled the rope, and no hour in which it could have sounded. Ivo was a corrections clerk. He had spent his life believing that a missing cause was an error someone could put right.

He found a way to restore the cause. The bell rang again. This time the child was never trapped, and the child's mother no longer remembered thanking the person who had saved him. Ivo kept the corrected record and the original side by side. He could not make them agree.<ref>[[Sovereign/History#The Reader|History, “The Reader”]]; [[Sovereign/Feats#3. The bell's cause — narrative|Feats, “The bell's cause”]].</ref>

Later accounts call him '''Sovereign'''. He does not like the title. What began with the bell became [[Sovereign/Self-Refinement|Self-Refinement]]: the ability to alter the description by which a threat identifies him, and eventually the description by which he identifies himself. Each revision can spare a life or escape a final sentence. Each also makes it harder to know whether the person who emerged is the person who entered.

<blockquote>"I can correct the page. I still have to answer to the people who lived on it."</blockquote>

== Before the name ==

Ivo grew up above a wet street with his mother Tala and younger sister Mira. Tala mended coats; Mira folded boats from receipts. He loved the ordinary proof that they were there: a voice in the next room, the chipped cup left beside the sink. He became a clerk because a line on a flood map could send a family toward safety or toward water. He also learned to mistake care for control. He could not leave an apology alone once it had been spoken, and a correction he made without checking the survey cost two families their homes.

His partner Sana Or saw both sides of him. Teren Oss, his closest friend, taught him to eat breakfast before trying to repair the city. Their lives did not become smaller when Ivo's power grew; his interventions made their memories and consent harder to protect. [[Sovereign/History|The history]] follows the events. [[Sovereign/Relationships|The relationships]] records what the people close to him lost and chose.<ref>[[Sovereign/History#The human|History, “The human”]]; [[Sovereign/Relationships|Relationships]].</ref>

== The work of revision ==

Ivo first learned to notice descriptions beneath events. He later changed events, then the rules that let an event count as his. As the Open Witness, he can question an attempted final definition when it leaves an accessible difference. This is the clerk's old habit at impossible scale: he lays two accounts together and asks where the lines fail to meet. [[The Unconditioned Draft|The Unruled Witness]] is the deeper state disclosed by the earliest dialogue and the Severance account: self-revision without a required trace, witness, substrate, or imported rule.

The clerk's usual process is not a wish. He examines a difference, forms a coherent change, and asks a witness to test what followed. A prepared revision can instead resolve during a closing act, even if no later trace survives. The peak state does not require either method. This distinction does not settle whether a successor has the same private consciousness: an escape can still preserve a new Ivo rather than the one who entered. [[Sovereign/Self-Refinement]] explains the timings; [[Sovereign/Axioms]] gives the archive's disputed rules; [[Sovereign/Feats]] distinguishes events from their interpretation.

The distinction between changing the world and changing himself matters. When Ivo diverts a flood, he changes an event, and other people bear the changed history. When he changes what a lethal order names as its defendant, he changes his own relation to the order. The order can still execute perfectly against the person it names. The harder question is whether the voice that answers afterward is continuous with that person. He has no instrument that can certify a first-person life from the outside.<ref>[[Sovereign/Self-Refinement#Eight kinds of edit|Self-Refinement, “Eight kinds of edit”]]; [[Sovereign/Feats#5. The lethal order — identity|Feats, “The lethal order”]].</ref>

